-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d7b9d3e-784c-586a-9879-40767c031372" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\ln 2 + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194275} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8aeb739-36a3-5843-95b5-cde0db730ec5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194273}] :question/id #uuid "e8bf8960-3077-5130-9de0-3e5c9b2bef5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-162944" :question/problem "Consider the transformation $f: R^{2} → R^{2}$, defined as\n\n$f(x) = \\begin{bmatrix}2x_{1}x_{2} \\\\ e^{x_{1}x_{2}}\\end{bmatrix}, x = \\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nIf the linear approximation of $f$ at $a = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ \\ln 2\\end{bmatrix}$ is given by\n\n$f(x) \\approx \\begin{bmatrix}∗ \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}2\\ln 2 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & 2\\end{bmatrix}(x - \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ \\ln 2\\end{bmatrix})$,\n\nwhat is the sum of the missing values?"}]}
